  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a binary string SSS, i.e. a string consisting of only the characters 000 and 111.\n\nYou can modify it by performing the following operation:\n\n\nChoose an index iii (1≤i≤N−31 \\leq i \\leq N-31≤i≤N−3) such that Si=Si+2S_i = S_{i+2}Si​=Si+2​, Si+1=Si+3S_{i+1} = S_{i+3}Si+1​=Si+3​, and Si≠Si+1S_i \\neq S_{i+1}Si​=Si+1​.\n\nThen, swap Si+1S_{i+1}Si+1​ and Si+2S_{i+2}Si+2​.\nOr, more simply, you can choose a substring equal to 0101\\text{0101}0101 and make it 0011\\text{0011}0011, or choose a substring equal to 1010\\text{1010}1010 and make it 1100\\text{1100}1100.\n\nCount the number of distinct binary strings you can make by performing this operation several (possibly, zero) times.\n\nThe answer can be large, so print it modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the length of the string.\nThe second line contains the binary string SSS.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of distinct binary strings that can be formed,  modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "Si∈{0,1}S_i \\in \\{0, 1\\}Si​∈{0,1}",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n5\n10010\n6\n101010\n12\n110101011010",
        "output": "1\n4\n12",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: No operation can be performed.\nTest case 222: The four binary strings that can be reached are:\n101010,110010,100110,101100101010, 110010, 100110, 101100101010,110010,100110,101100.\nTest case 333: The binary strings that can be obtained are:\n110101011010,111001011010,110011011010,110110011010110101011010, 111001011010, 110011011010, 110110011010110101011010,111001011010,110011011010,110110011010\n110100111010,110101011100,111000111010,111001011100110100111010, 110101011100, 111000111010, 111001011100110100111010,110101011100,111000111010,111001011100\n110011011100,110110011100,110100111100,111000111100110011011100, 110110011100, 110100111100, 111000111100110011011100,110110011100,110100111100,111000111100"
      }
